capability sql-mysql/autocommit  each statement left uncommitted until a commit, by the session's setting
  heroes  refused: `begin` opens a transaction where one is wanted, so a statement never stays uncommitted by a setting nobody sees; `exec(@db, "SET autocommit = 0", [])` remains the server's to run
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Connection.autocommit, Connection.get_autocommit
  note    PEP 249 opens a transaction implicitly; Go's `database/sql` does not

capability sql-mysql/charset  the connection's character set and collation chosen
  heroes  refused: the connection speaks `utf8mb4`, the one set that holds every character a Heroes `str` holds; a column of another set is converted by the server
  go      Charset, Config.Collation
  rust    -
  python  Connection (charset, collation), Connection.set_character_set, Connection.set_charset, Connection.character_set_name, charset
  note    collation 45, `utf8mb4_general_ci`, which MySQL 5.5 to 9 and MariaDB know

capability sql-mysql/time-zone  instants read and written in UTC whatever the server's zone
  heroes  mysql.open
  go      Config.Loc, Config.ParseTime, TimeTruncate
  rust    -
  python  Connection (init_command)
  note    the session's `time_zone` is set to `+00:00` on opening, so a `TIMESTAMP` comes in UTC; a `DATETIME`, which holds no zone, is read as UTC

